Revision history for MCP-Picnic

{{$NEXT}}
    - Tool results keep non-ASCII characters intact: product names,
      addresses and prices such as "Müsli" or "€" reached the client as
      mojibake because the JSON payload was UTF-8 encoded twice
    - The 2FA login no longer gets stuck: when the SMS request fails, or a
      verification fails because the code expired, the next tool call logs
      in again and requests a fresh code instead of reporting a pending
      verification forever (also for POST /api/auth/verify-2fa)
    - mcp-picnic-http: clients can be required to authenticate. With
      MCP_PICNIC_TOKEN set, /api/* and /mcp answer 401 unless the request
      carries "Authorization: Bearer <token>" (compared in constant time);
      /openapi.json declares the matching bearer security scheme
    - mcp-picnic-http: listens on http://127.0.0.1:3000 by default instead
      of every interface (-l / MOJO_LISTEN still choose another address)
    - mcp-picnic-http: without MCP_PICNIC_TOKEN it refuses to start on a
      non-loopback address and answers 403 to requests from other hosts or
      relayed by a proxy. Deployments that listen on http://*:3000 or sit
      behind a reverse proxy now have to set MCP_PICNIC_TOKEN

0.001     2026-09-18 19:29:01Z
    - Initial release
    - MCP server exposing the Picnic Supermarket API (via WWW::Picnic)
      to AI assistants such as Claude
    - Interactive 2FA login flow
    - Tools: search_products, get_product_details, get_suggestions,
      get_cart, add_to_cart, remove_from_cart, clear_cart,
      get_delivery_slots, set_delivery_slot, get_user, get_categories
    - HTTP server variant (mcp-picnic-http) for remote MCP and a REST API
